✅ 11. Demonstrate BLOCKED using synchronized

11.1 Definition

A thread enters the BLOCKED state when:

🔴 It is trying to enter a synchronized block or method.
🔴 Another thread already owns the monitor lock.

The BLOCKED thread waits until the lock becomes available.

11.2 Why Do We Need BLOCKED?

Suppose two threads want to update the same bank account.
🔴 Thread-A → Update Balance
🔴 Thread-B → Update Balance

If both execute simultaneously:
Balance = 1000
Thread-A → +500
Thread-B → -200

The final balance may become incorrect due to race conditions.

To prevent this:

synchronized(account){
    // Update Balance
}

🔴 Only one thread can enter the synchronized block at a time.
🔴 The other thread waits in the BLOCKED state.

11.3 How Does a Thread Enter BLOCKED?

Flow:

